ccextractor compiled to WebAssembly for TS Inspector
===================================================

Source: https://github.com/CCExtractor/ccextractor.git
Commit: 97b381a2b0bee35d3b22411772329eb540ee511b
Licence: GPL-2.0-only (see LICENSE.txt in this directory)
Built with Emscripten, flags in scripts/build_wasm.py.

The files ccextractor.js and ccextractor.wasm here are that build. They are
bundled into dist/ts-inspector.html, so a distributed page is, as a
whole, under GPL-2.0. Whoever hosts that page must offer this source
from the same place. The TS Inspector sources are MIT; build with
`python3 build.py --no-gpl` to leave these modules, and FFmpeg, out.

Rebuild with: python3 scripts/build_wasm.py --only ccextractor
